## Johnny-Five persistent memory

Johnny-Five is the primary persistent memory store. Its global Codex hooks already recall project-scoped context at task start, search on corrections and risky edits, preserve a pre-compaction floor, and enforce memory discipline.

- Scope every manual memory call to the repository's main checkout, as the hooks do: `J5_PROJECT_DIR` when set, else the parent of `git rev-parse --path-format=absolute --git-common-dir`. Never pass a git worktree's own path or hardcode another project's path.
- Search before investigation, authoring decisions, corrections, and stores. Update an existing memory instead of creating a duplicate.
- Use the single canonical SSE service at `http://127.0.0.1:8787/sse/` in the container named `johnny-five`.
- Never launch a native stdio Johnny-Five process or another container against `/data/memory.db`.
- If the service is restored after a task starts without J5 tools, start a fresh Codex task to reload the MCP inventory.
<!-- END johnny-five-codex -->
